WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.500
Hello, Internet! Welcome to Film Theory, the show that knows that translucent doesn't mean invisible, it means semi-transparent.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.200
So, how about The Boys, huh?

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:16.800
Back in the late 2010s, a time when superheroes ruled the pop culture roost, this Amazon TV series burst through the wall and said no.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.400
Trust me, you do not want these guys to be real.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.700
If you aren't familiar, The Boys is a satirical series that imagines what a world with superheroes would really look like.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.000
And oh man, is this show a bloody good time in a lot of different ways.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:36.600
And while there are tons of smaller heroes with superpowers in this world, the biggest and most popular of them all team up into a supergroup known as The Seven.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.900
And these guys aren't the type of heroes that you'd expect.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.100
No, they're not Boy Scouts or friendly neighborhood warriors, they're corrupt.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:47.200
They're self-serving and they're dealing with real-world problems like addiction, insecurity, and egotism.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.300
Killing most criminals in their crosshairs, as well as plenty of innocents along the way.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.500
The world of this series is incredible.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.400
But today, I wanted to take a look at one very specific hero.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.800
The biggest and definitely baddest one of them all, Homelander.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.800
I'm not just like the rest of you.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.300
I'm stronger, I'm smarter, I'm better.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.000
I am better!

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.800
Homelander is basically this world's version of all the oldest superhero tropes.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:14.700
He can fly, he's super strong and fast, he's basically invulnerable, and he has himself heat vision.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.500
All while literally being wrapped in an American flag.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.100
And this is why Homelander caught the attention of my theorist brain so quickly.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.900
In this show that leans so heavily on the realistic consequences of superheroes,

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:28.600
got me wondering, just how super is this superest of supes?

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:31.200
And by that I mean, how strong is Homelander?

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:35.000
Given what we see him do across the series, what are some real numbers to Homelander's power?

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.800
And what would his biggest strength be?

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:38.900
Well, loyal theorists, here's the craziest part.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:43.400
The thing that I think is Homelander's biggest strength definitely isn't what you'd expect.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.700
And I also think it's his biggest weakness.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:51.300
And knowing what that is, is gonna tell us a lot about where the story of the boys is headed in future seasons.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.500
But before we hop into the strength of this megacorporation superhero,

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:59.000
let's talk about the strength of our latest round of theorywear, the Northern Lights Collection.

