And I gotta say, I think we've managed to do it.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.900
So please, go check out the Northern Lights collection over at TheoryWear.com.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:24.100
But that's enough shameless self-promotion for now. Let's get back to The Boys, shall we?

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:29.300
So to figure out what Homelander's most powerful abilities are, I figure that we need to first decide which powers we're actually gonna measure.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:33.100
For today's purposes, I've narrowed it down to the three that I think are his most iconic.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.600
Super strength, how fast he can move, and heat vision.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:40.800
So let's just look at the science behind each of these and see what we can dig up, starting with Homelander's super strength.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:48.000
So far, the boys have really held back from showing Homelander undergoing the sorts of godlike feats of strength that we typically see in other superhero shows.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:54.300
He hasn't lifted a car with one finger, or stopped a building from collapsing, or held a boat together with his bare hands, or anything like that.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.800
Now, that's not to say that he couldn't do things like that.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:05.000
When it's suggested that he save an airplane full of passengers from crashing, his reasons for not doing it have nothing to do with a lack of strength, but rather a lack of things to stand on.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.100
Lift the plane up.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:09.100
Lift the plane? How? There's nothing to stand on.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:15.000
But if he were standing on solid ground, assuming it's at its maximum takeoff load, lifting this Boeing 737

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:21.969
means that Homelander could shoulder 430,000 pounds, or about 195,000 kilograms, no problem.

00:04:21.969 --> 00:04:27.944
And if we want to bring comic evidence into this, that version of Homelander was able to grab an F-16 fighter jet weighing roughly

00:04:27.944 --> 00:04:34.600
20,000 pounds, or 9,200 kilograms, with a single hand and easily toss it across an airport hangar in annoyance.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:38.816
All that said, we do see other feats of strength throughout the show, with Homelander casually throwing people around

00:04:38.816 --> 00:04:43.600
like it's nothing, physically punching through human bodies, crushing human skulls like a nut.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:49.500
It is all very violent and very gruesome and very YouTube unfriendly, so you're just gonna have to trust me on all this.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:54.400
Just from these feats of strength alone, we can get an idea of how crazy powerful Homelander actually is.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:05:02.800
One study stated that crushing a human skull would require up to 1,200 pounds of force, which would be like putting your head inside of a hydraulic press machine.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:07.200
And this was something that Homelander did with a single hand while distracted.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:14.700
As for punching through a human chest, unsurprisingly, it's difficult to find information about how much force you need to break through the human sternum with the human fist.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.400
I wonder why that might be hard to find. Go figure.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:22.700
But you know what? We don't actually need those numbers to calculate the wild strength that Homelander demonstrates in this one scene.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:26.500
As he pulls his fist out of this guy, much to his annoyance, it's covered in blood.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:32.800
That means that his punch actually broke through the skin, which takes a lot more force for a blunt object than you might expect.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:36.900
It takes roughly 100 pounds per square inch of pressure to puncture through human skin.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:46.700
And given that a human fist is roughly 64 square inches in surface area, that means that Homelander needed to apply 6,400 PSI on this dude in order to get his hand bloody.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:55.500
An average boxer, by comparison, can deliver between 1,200 and 1,700 PSI, which is basically the same level of pressure as an industrial pressure washer.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:59.300
Now imagine that, but three times worse, and it was nothing to Homelander.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:02.200
And if you think that's scary, it's not even the most strength that we see him using.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:09.000
In the very first scene of the show, we see Homelander casually tossing a bank robber away after saving two kids that he was holding at gunpoint.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:12.900
I was actually able to figure out roughly where the scene takes place, thanks to the street signs.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:18.300
Going through it frame by frame, you can see signs for Borum Place and Smith Street, real locations in Brooklyn, New York.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:22.200
Thankfully, this means that we're able to get a pretty good idea of how far Homelander threw the thug,

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:27.900
since a standard New York City block is about 264 feet by 900 feet, or about 80 meters by 274.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:32.300
Using that, I was able to estimate that the robber was thrown about 135 feet.

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:38.200
He was in the air for roughly 6.1 seconds, and plugging all of that into a projectile motion calculator,

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:43.700
we'll find that he was thrown at about 68 miles an hour, 30.5 meters a second.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:48.700
Assuming that this dude weighed as much as an average American male, and plugging all of that into a kinetic energy formula,

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:53.700
we'll find that Homelander threw this guy with a wild 42,000 joules of energy.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:58.900
To give you a frame of reference, that would be 26 times harder than boxing legend Mike Tyson can punch.

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:04.400
Okay, so Homelander's physical strength is incredible, but that doesn't matter a whole lot if he's not fast enough to land a punch.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:10.400
But don't you worry, my friends, he is more than fast enough to land a blow that'll rip through someone's chest easily.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:14.500
Both on foot and flying through the air, Homelander is tremendously fast.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:18.400
We see this clearly demonstrated the multiple times he catches up with planes mid-flight,

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:21.700
but that is nowhere near Homelander's most impressive feat of speed.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:24.900
Nope, that honor goes to this scene from the finale of Season 1.

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:29.200
After confronting Boys Leader Billy Butcher in a house that's been rigged with C4 explosives,

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:32.300
Butcher detonates them, hoping to hurt Homelander and himself.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:38.100
However, Homelander is able to move quickly enough not only to save himself from the explosive blast, but Butcher as well.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:43.900
C4's velocity of detonation, or the rate at which it explodes, is about 26,400 feet a second.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:48.700
That is 18,000 miles per hour, 29,000 kilometers an hour.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:51.600
Now, you can obviously tell that that is ludicrously fast,

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:56.100
but moving that quickly also means that Homelander would be creating bone-crunching amounts of energy.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:58.600
Using the equation force equals mass times acceleration,

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:04.900
we can figure out that Homelander is generating a crazy 700,000 newtons of force just from moving.

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:09.500
Now, that might be nothing to Homelander, but you gotta remember, he's also moving Butcher at this speed,

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:11.100
which would almost certainly kill him,

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:15.800
because that force is roughly 10 times worse than what you'd feel during a 40 mile per hour head-on crash.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:19.600
So in saving Butcher in the scene, Homelander actually kind of killed him,

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:22.500
which, you know, would save him a lot of trouble further in the series.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.600
While super speed and physical strength are both wildly powerful abilities,

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:31.000
the flashiest of Homelander's superpowers and the one he leans on the most is undoubtedly his laser vision.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.700
In fact, he uses it so much, and it's such a big part of the show's marketing,

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.200
that I'd classify this as his signature ability.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:38.000
But just how powerful is it?

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.600
Is it the strongest ability?

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:43.600
After all, we see him do everything from use it to melt guns to cut through humans like they're butter.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:48.300
So to calculate what I figured would be the upper range of the amount of energy Homelander can output through his eyes,

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:52.900
I decided to use this scene where he cuts through a private jet in just 0.96 seconds.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:56.300
How'd I figure it out? Well, there's a lot of complicated math, but here's the long and short of it.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:09:00.400
We were able to figure out that the plane used in the scene was a British Aerospace 125,

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:03.600
and though we couldn't find the exact materials this model of plane is made from,

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.900
most commercial aircraft are made using aluminum, titanium, and steel.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:11.400
We're just gonna be using aluminum to keep things simple, and to underestimate his power in this case.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.800
Using the Aerospace's height, length, and hull thickness,

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:20.800
we were able to estimate that he was able to melt roughly 115.7 kilograms of aluminum in that 0.9 seconds.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:21.700
Insane!

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:25.000
Using the average width of a pair of human eyes as the size of our laser beams,

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:29.600
assuming that the hull is made of aluminum, and that the temperature of the hull is about negative 40 degrees Celsius,

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:32.800
or the warmer end of the outside of an airplane at cruising altitude,

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:37.600
with some back-in-the-napkin math, we can calculate that Homelander's less than one second of heat vision here

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:44.600
transferred a massive 73,052,980 joules of energy directly to the metal on that plane.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:50.400
That is over 20 kilowatt hours, or a little less than what you'd need to power an average house for an entire day,

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:54.600
all from Homelander just looking at something really hard for less than a second.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:59.800
And believe it or not, all of these assumptions were actually just low-balling the amount of energy Homelander's outputting in the scene.

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:02.200
We were giving him the easiest possible scenario here.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:06.600
And it's also not saying anything about his ability to control the intensity of those eye-beams.

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:10.800
He's able to heat up a bottle of milk without melting the bottle or boiling the liquid.

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:15.800
That right there tells us that Homelander is just really good at figuring out the thermodynamics of objects around him,

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:22.300
knowing how much energy his eye-beams need to output to heat milk, but also to melt aluminum depending on the circumstance.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:28.000
That is an insane amount of control, and probably a stronger ability than just lifting things or moving fast.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:31.300
So it is clear that Homelander is just ridiculously powerful.

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:33.900
But here's the thing. While his physical prowess is unmatched,

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:37.900
I actually don't believe that that's what makes Homelander the most powerful of superheroes.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:42.900
Instead, Homelander's biggest strength, the thing that makes him the most powerful and the scariest of all the Supes,

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:44.600
it's his brand. Let me explain.

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:50.100
Superheroes are big business in the real world, with the corporations who own them bringing in billions from those IP.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:56.600
In 2013 alone, the most popular superheroes generated between 275 million and 1.3 billion each,

00:10:56.600 --> 00:11:00.900
just from merchandise retail sales alone, in a single year.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:05.400
As the most powerful Supe in the world and the leader of the seven, between movies and action figures and whatever,

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:10.400
Homelander's brand should easily be making at least the lower end of that margin within the world of The Boys.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:14.800
And that's not even considering the military contracts that Homelander's able to bring in for the Vought Company.

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:19.600
Additionally, it's very clear that Supes in this universe function very similar to real-world influencers,

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:21.700
and they have way more power than you might think.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:25.900
First of all, if we want to continue the cash talk, they can command huge sums of money in multiple ways.

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:30.100
Popular athletes and YouTubers are often worth tens or even hundreds of millions of dollars.

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:35.400
Multiple soccer players were offered $1 billion contracts that they turned down, by the way,

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:36.800
because as one article put it, quote,

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:40.500
Most soccer fans around the world now follow players, not teams.

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:46.300
Which makes a lot of sense when you consider that two of these players have between 100 and 480 million social media followers.

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:52.600
That's in the same range as the 193 million followers that Starlight has in the world of The Boys over on Instagram.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:57.500
And though she's touted as the most followed Supe, Homelander has to have himself similar numbers.

00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:01.700
Building off of that, these insane follower counts give influencers massive amounts of power.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:07.300
Oh sure, MrBeast was able to leverage his subscriber base to get Beast Burger into the $100 million revenue range,

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:13.100
but what's even more impressive was that he was able to keep the Feastables chocolate bar displays in retail stores clean

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:15.900
simply by asking fans to tidy them up for him.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:19.800
Which they did, all without pay, just because he asked them nicely.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:23.600
And it's not just their own stuff that these influencers can push their followers towards.

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:26.700
They are able to get their followers to buy other people's stuff too.

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:29.900
According to an advertiser report from Precise TV and Giraffe Insights,

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:33.200
almost half of teens remember seeing ads on platforms like YouTube.

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:38.400
60% consider watching them instead of skipping the ad, and 70% have bought something that they've seen.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:43.900
Heck, if you want to take money out of this entirely, 86% of young Americans want to become social media influencers

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:47.100
because they look up to people like YouTubers and TikTokers.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:50.900
And this is definitely the way that Supes like Homelander are treated in The Boys.

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:54.100
I mean, just look at the interaction that Homelander has with the two kids that he saves.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:55.000
You boys okay?

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:56.000
Can I get a selfie?

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:56.900
Of course you can.

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:59.900
This isn't the way people react after being saved from a bank robbery.

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:03.600
This is how people react when meeting a celebrity they adore and look up to.

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:04.800
But this doesn't even stop there.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:09.000
Given all of this, all the power that Homelander's accrued through money and cultural influence,

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.200
that's not even the thing that gives him the most power.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:15.400
Because he also has the full backing of a multi-billion dollar conglomerate.

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:18.700
By the end of Season 3 of The Boys, Homelander takes control of Vought International,

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:23.300
installing Ashley Barrett, somebody he considers a close ally that he can control, as CEO.

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:28.800
In essence, this gives Homelander CEO control of the corporation that not only owns the legal entity that is his brand,

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:32.100
but also most other licensed superheroes throughout the world.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:37.100
And there is no overselling just how much power or how many resources this affords Homelander.

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:40.800
In 2018, 14 of the top 30 most powerful people in the world,

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:43.400
ranked by Forbes, were executives at conglomerates,

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:46.300
right there alongside leaders of world superpowers.

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.400
And given the social media marketing for The Boys,

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:52.700
Vought is using all of its power to make sure Homelander's reputation is upheld.

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:55.800
He's got a propaganda machine at his fingertips.

00:13:55.800 --> 00:14:01.100
In the coming months, Homelander will stand trial for saving his son from a vicious, starlight-loving thug.

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:04.100
An act of heroism, now somehow being branded a murder.

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:08.200
Make no mistake, Vought and its shareholders stand fully behind Homelander.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.800
Really, at this point, there's only one place left for Homelander to go.

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:13.200
Only one place that he could get even stronger.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:17.800
I believe that next season, Homelander is gonna run for President of the United States.

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:19.600
Now, if that sounds outlandish, it shouldn't.

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:23.300
This didn't happen in the comics, but the show's already diverged a lot from that story,

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:24.700
so it's clearly doing its own thing.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:27.300
Plus, there's already an election going on in the world of The Boys.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:32.300
And think about how much time the show's devoted to Homelander caring so much about where he sat with his base.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.500
-"21 points."

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:34.700
-"They loved your speech?"

